IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pl-types`
IMPORT `pl-eligibility`
IMPORT `pl-leave`
IMPORT `pl-protection`
IMPORT `pl-payments`

-- Parental Leave and Employment Protection Act 1987 — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.
--
--   "For this person and this child, which leave may the person take and for
--    how long; are they entitled to parental leave payments, at what weekly
--    rate, for how many weeks, with how many weeks of preterm baby payment;
--    and by when must they apply?"
--
-- One answer through Goals 1, 2 and 4 (pl-eligibility.l4, pl-leave.l4,
-- pl-payments.l4). Notices, the position and protection (Goal 3) answer
-- their own questions in pl-protection.l4.

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Parental leave position` HAS
    `the employment test met`                           IS AN `Employment test`
    `the primary carer`                                 IS A `Primary carer kind`
    `may take primary carer leave`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `primary carer leave, in weeks`                     IS A NUMBER
    `may take partner's leave`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `partner's leave, in weeks`                         IS A NUMBER
    `extended leave still available, in weeks`          IS A NUMBER
    `may request negotiated carer leave`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `entitled to parental leave payments`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `weekly rate of parental leave payment`             IS A NUMBER
    `weeks of parental leave payment`                   IS A NUMBER
    `weeks of preterm baby payment`                     IS A NUMBER
    `last day to apply for payments`                    IS A MAYBE DATE

-- The employment test, for an employee.
@ref s 2BA(1)
GIVEN c IS A `Parental leave case`
GIVETH AN `Employment test`
`the employment test for` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `employment, if an employee`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `neither employment test`
    WHEN JUST e THEN `the employment test met by` e `before` (`the date the tests look back from, for` (c's `the child concerned`))

@ref ss 2BA, 7, 8, 9, 17, 19, 23, 26, 30B, 71D, 71DA, 71I, 71J, 71M; Schedule 1AA cl 5
@export default The parental leave position under the Parental Leave and Employment Protection Act 1987 (NZ) for one person and one child: the employment test met (s 2BA), whether the person is the primary carer (s 7), whether they may take primary carer leave (up to 26 weeks, s 8), partner's leave (1 or 2 weeks, ss 17, 19) and how much extended leave is left (ss 23-28), whether they may request negotiated carer leave (s 30B), and whether they are entitled to parental leave payments (s 71D), at what weekly rate (s 71M), for 26 weeks plus any preterm baby payment weeks (ss 71J, 71DA), and the last day to apply (s 71I). Children due, born or taken into care before 1 July 2020 are refused. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Parental leave case`  @desc The child (expected and actual birth, the day the 36th week would end, the date of becoming the primary carer), who the person is (s 7), their employment with the employer, their spouse or partner's employment test, the leave already taken, the payment facts, and any return to work
GIVETH A `Parental leave position`
`the parental leave position for` c MEANS
    IF   NOT `this version applies to` child
    THEN `a child due, born or taken into care before 1 July 2020 is outside this version of the Act`
    ELSE `Parental leave position` WITH
            `the employment test met`                   IS test
            `the primary carer`                         IS `the primary carer kind of` (c's `the carer facts`)
            `may take primary carer leave`              IS pcl
            `primary carer leave, in weeks`             IS IF pcl THEN 26 ELSE 0
            `may take partner's leave`                  IS partner
            `partner's leave, in weeks`                 IS IF partner THEN `the partner's leave, in weeks, for` test ELSE 0
            `extended leave still available, in weeks`  IS
                IF   (`is the primary carer` (c's `the carer facts`) OR c's `is the primary carer's spouse or partner and assumes care`)
                     AND NOT `s 6 bars parental leave in` c
                THEN `the extended leave remaining, in weeks, own test` test `, partner's test` (c's `the spouse or partner's employment test`) `, history` (c's `the leave history`)
                ELSE 0
            `may request negotiated carer leave`        IS `may request negotiated carer leave, entitled to primary carer leave:` pcl `, to payments if on leave:` paid
            `entitled to parental leave payments`       IS paid
            `weekly rate of parental leave payment`     IS IF paid THEN `the weekly rate of parental leave payment` (c's `the payment facts`) ELSE 0
            `weeks of parental leave payment`           IS IF paid THEN `the weeks of parental leave payment` ELSE 0
            `weeks of preterm baby payment`             IS `the weeks of preterm baby payment for` child `, entitled to parental leave payments:` paid
            `last day to apply for payments`            IS
                IF   child's `born to the person or their spouse or partner`
                THEN CONSIDER child's `date of birth`
                     WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                     WHEN JUST b THEN JUST (`the last day to apply for payments, child` child `, returned to work` (c's `returned to work on`))
                ELSE JUST (`the last day to apply for payments, child` child `, returned to work` (c's `returned to work on`))
    WHERE
        child   MEANS c's `the child concerned`
        test    MEANS `the employment test for` c
        pcl     MEANS `may take primary carer leave, case` c `, test met` test
        partner MEANS `may take partner's leave, case` c `, test met` test
        paid    MEANS `entitled to parental leave payments` c

`a child due, born or taken into care before 1 July 2020 is outside this version of the Act` MEANS
    REFUSE "a child due, born or taken into care before 1 July 2020 falls under the Act as it stood before the 2017 amendments, which this encoding does not carry"
